enchilada: GPU: no DIAG panics on a failed BO mapping; the ioctl fails instead

With CoreAnimation driving the GPU (backboardd through libsweetca), a 12 MiB BO (one 1125x2436
surface) at iova 0x87ab9000 ran past 0x88000000, the end of what the 64 L3 tables of the PTE pool
cover, and mapGem() hit its "SWEET DIAG: mapGem page N of 3072" panic. Both DIAG panics in
mapGem() - no iova left, and a page that cannot be entered (no page table, pa 0 or misaligned) -
are reachable from any client's GEM_NEW / SURFACE_BO, so a resource limit killed the phone. They
now log the same facts (size, page, iova, pa, arena pa) with IOLog, undo the pages already
entered and the address range, and fail the call: kIOReturnNoSpace without an iova,
kIOReturnNoMemory for a page; gemNew() and surfaceBo() already release the slot, the descriptor
and the arena pages on that path. The loop no longer counts the failed page as mapped. These
were the only panic() calls in SweetAdreno.cpp, and sweet_gpu.c has none. Mesa 25.0.7 does not
check every heap allocation (fd_bo_heap_alloc -> fd_bo_ref(NULL)), so the client may still
crash; that is recoverable, a kernel panic is not. The table limit itself is 0196.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
@@ -380,13 +380,12 @@
 		iova = setIova;
 		taken = size;
 	} else if (!sweet_gpu_iova_alloc(size, &iova, &taken)) {
-		IOLog("SWEET GPU: no GPU address space for %llu bytes\n", size);
-		panic("SWEET DIAG: no iova for %llu bytes (arena %#llx)", size, slot->pa);
+		/* The client's ioctl fails; it must not take the phone down (0195: was a DIAG panic). */
+		IOLog("SWEET GPU: no GPU address space for %llu bytes (arena %#llx)\n", size, slot->pa);
+		return kIOReturnNoSpace;
 	}
-	bool ok = true;
-	uint64_t mapped = 0;
-	for (; mapped < size && ok; mapped += GPU_PAGE) {     /* K2(a): every 4 KiB PTE, not every 16 KiB */
-		uint64_t pa;
+	uint64_t mapped = 0, pa = 0;
+	for (; mapped < size; mapped += GPU_PAGE) {     /* K2(a): every 4 KiB PTE, not every 16 KiB */
 		if (slot->pa != 0) {
 			/* GEM_NEW: the arena address is already known, no descriptor walk needed. */
 			pa = slot->pa + mapped;
@@ -394,16 +393,17 @@
 			IOByteCount length = 0;
 			pa = (uint64_t)slot->md->getPhysicalSegment(mapped, &length, kIOMemoryMapperNone);
 		}
-		ok = pa != 0 && (pa & (GPU_PAGE - 1)) == 0 && sweet_gpu_vm_map(iova + mapped, pa, ro);
-		if (!ok) {
-			panic("SWEET DIAG: mapGem page %llu of %llu: iova %#llx pa %#llx arena %#llx",
-			    mapped / GPU_PAGE, size / GPU_PAGE, iova, pa, slot->pa);
+		if (pa == 0 || (pa & (GPU_PAGE - 1)) != 0 || !sweet_gpu_vm_map(iova + mapped, pa, ro)) {
+			break;
 		}
 	}
-	if (!ok) {
+	if (mapped < size) {
+		/* Pages [0, mapped) are in; undo them and the address range, then fail the call (was a DIAG panic). */
 		sweet_gpu_vm_unmap(iova, mapped);
 		sweet_gpu_iova_free(iova, taken);
-		IOLog("SWEET GPU: cannot map %llu bytes into the GPU address space (page %llu)\n", size, mapped / GPU_PAGE);
+		IOLog("SWEET GPU: cannot map %llu bytes into the GPU address space: page %llu of %llu, "
+		    "iova %#llx pa %#llx (arena %#llx)\n", size, mapped / GPU_PAGE, size / GPU_PAGE,
+		    iova + mapped, pa, slot->pa);
 		return kIOReturnNoMemory;
 	}
 	slot->iova = iova;
